exports[`internal workflow preview > previews four sorted workflows as twelve host files with exact canonical bodies and sidecars 1`] = `
{
  ".agents/skills/devai-backlog-harvest/SKILL.md": "---
name: devai-backlog-harvest
description: Harvest unresolved work from this session's context, memory and worktree artifacts in a DEVAI-governed repo into deduplicated GitHub issue drafts; register them only when explicitly asked. Use for "what did we leave open", "turn these findings into issues".
license: Apache-2.0
compatibility: Needs the GitHub CLI authenticated for the target repository.
metadata:
  devai-status: stable
  devai-workflow-schema: '1'
---

# devai-backlog-harvest

Runs inline: it needs this conversation's context, so never run it in a forked subagent.

Resolve the target repository, then scan the requested sources (session, round, campaign artifacts, memory as pointers) for unresolved findings, deferred scope, unanswered decisions, risks, workarounds and follow-ups. Verify current state — artifacts, open and closed issues, PRs — before treating an old concern as open; split confirmed-open, resolved, and unverifiable.

Per candidate: source locator (host/session/time/file-line or digest), symptom, current impact, evidence, component, blocking status, closure condition. Keep severity, certainty and urgency separate; a decision stays a decision and names whose answer is needed.

Search open and relevant closed issues and PRs, paginating the full scope; match by behavior, component and identifiers. One issue per coherent actionable outcome; link related items; split independently deliverable work. Redact secrets and private transcript detail. Draft title and body with the repository template; owner, labels and milestone stay proposed until verified.

Output: ready-to-post bodies, a source → issue map, and exclusions with reasons. "Inspect" or "draft" means prepare locally. "Register" or "open" means create through the authenticated GitHub tool, verify number, URL and body, and never bulk-update, close or assign unrelated issues; after an uncertain outcome, inspect state before retrying.
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-backlog-harvest/agents/openai.yaml": "interface:
  display_name: 'DEVAI backlog harvest'
  short_description: 'Harvest unresolved work into issue drafts'
policy:
  allow_implicit_invocation: true
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-campaign/SKILL.md": "---
name: devai-campaign
description: Status, planning and readiness for DEVAI campaigns, rounds and tasks in a DEVAI-governed repo (DEVAI, STYNX, DETRAN) — where things stand, what blocks, a grounded ETA, a campaign draft from open issues, or whether a round can close, seal or release.
license: Apache-2.0
compatibility: Needs the project-local @aarusso-nyx/devai package and the GitHub CLI for the plan route.
metadata:
  devai-status: stable
  devai-workflow-schema: '1'
---

# devai-campaign

First, collect read-only facts: \`git rev-parse --show-toplevel\`, \`git remote get-url origin\`, \`git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\`, \`git rev-parse --short HEAD\` and \`git status --short\`, then the live round state under \`.devai/state/\`: the rounds with runtime state (\`.devai/state/round-runs/<round>/\`), each round's live controller (\`controller.json\`) and dispatch journal (\`dispatch-journal.jsonl\`), and the task records (\`.devai/state/tasks/<task>.json\`). There is no single current-round pointer; name the round you report on. Run nothing that builds, tests or writes. If the collector fails, say so and continue with what you can read — never guess a HEAD, round id or candidate.

Pick one route from the request.

## status

Lead with stage, done, blocked, next action, with campaign → round → task identifiers. Keep implemented, tested, reviewed, merged, released, closed and sealed as separate states; a PASS in one says nothing about the others. Evidence is receipts, task reports, CI and closure records; a session summary is a lead, not proof. Do not run builds or validations to answer status — name the missing evidence. ETA from observed durations of comparable tasks in this campaign; a best/likely/worst range only when evidence supports one, otherwise the next bounded milestone and "full ETA not yet estimable". Never infer completion from token use or a percentage. Budget, when it matters: source, unit, window, usage, cap or waiver — never mixing cached input, output, provider quota and campaign accounting.

## plan

Fetch the complete requested issue set (paginate; record query time and ids) and inspect linked decisions, PRs and current plans. Coverage table: every issue → planned work | existing active round | duplicate/resolved (with evidence) | explicit deferral | blocked on an Owner or upstream decision. Group by outcome and dependency; order rounds by prerequisite and risk. Per task, only the fields the round runner consumes (\`law/policy/round-execution.json\`); unapproved architecture or Owner choices are marked _proposed_; settled decisions are preserved. Keep upstream DEVAI/STYNX changes and DETRAN adoption proofs separate. Drafting authorizes nothing: no issue-state changes, commits, dispatch or publication; revalidate the issue snapshot before execution.

## readiness

Name the endpoint: close, seal, merge, tag, release, or adopter-ready. Effect table: permitted now / candidate SHA or tree / prerequisites / protected approval remaining. Reconcile candidate identity, required checks, reviewer receipts, exports and version populations; run cheap deterministic preflight before long gates. A code-assessor verdict is evidence bound to its commit and rubric hash, never authorization; a stale or mismatched one is ignored. Keep closed, sealed, merged, tagged, published and adopted distinct; a close with transferred criteria keeps their real outcomes visible. Stop on a changed candidate or an unmet protected approval and name the exact blocked action.

## Decisions

When a route surfaces an unresolved Owner decision, present it with the host's question form: the concrete problem, mutually exclusive options, your recommendation, and what each option changes in behavior, scope, effort and effects. Record the literal answer in the campaign record when writing is authorized. Silence, a default, or time elapsed is not an answer.

Boundary: read-only unless the request authorizes a write through a DEVAI action. A readiness verdict is evidence, not permission.
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-campaign/agents/openai.yaml": "interface:
  display_name: 'DEVAI campaign'
  short_description: 'Status, planning and readiness for DEVAI campaigns'
policy:
  allow_implicit_invocation: false
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-resource-control/SKILL.md": "---
name: devai-resource-control
description: Apply an explicit Owner change to a DEVAI token budget, waiver, model or effort assignment for a task, round or campaign, preserving scope, duration and accounting. Use when the Owner says raise or waive the budget, use a cheaper model, lower effort, or re-steer resources.
license: Apache-2.0
compatibility: Needs the project-local @aarusso-nyx/devai package.
metadata:
  devai-status: stable
  devai-workflow-schema: '1'
---

# devai-resource-control

Identify which limit the instruction means: campaign/round/task allocation, runtime goal budget, or provider account quota (a skill cannot waive a provider quota or reset account usage). Read the governing plan, the budget record and the instruction itself.

Resolve: the new cap or waived state, affected ids, effective time, duration (one occasion | rest of round | rest of campaign | until revoked), expiry. Apply through the existing budget/assignment mechanism and record format. A prospective change never rewrites a historical FAIL into PASS; previous windows and overruns stay. When a runtime limit needs a user-controlled host setting, say exactly which control and stop — a plan-file edit does not change the runtime.

Keep model/effort changes separate from budget unless the instruction includes both. Confirm the model is available locally; don't turn a steering instruction into a permanent default. Reduce cost through bounded reading, smaller packets, focused checks and valid evidence reuse — never by accepting defects, skipping required security or product evidence, or widening write scopes. Parallel work gets non-overlapping owned paths, locks, ceilings and an integration owner; dispatch only when the current session rules allow it.

Output: old → new, scope, expiry, what was applied, what could not be and why, remaining restrictions. Reuse the decision within its scope on later turns without asking again.
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-resource-control/agents/openai.yaml": "interface:
  display_name: 'DEVAI resource control'
  short_description: 'Apply an explicit budget, model or effort change'
policy:
  allow_implicit_invocation: false
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-review-control/SKILL.md": "---
name: devai-review-control
description: Review-cycle exceptions and stalled reviews in DEVAI-governed repos — permission for an extra cycle, cycle limits, retry-versus-cycle accounting, convergence diagnosis, reviewer packets. Not for ordinary code review.
license: Apache-2.0
compatibility: Needs the project-local @aarusso-nyx/devai package.
metadata:
  devai-status: stable
  devai-workflow-schema: '1'
---

# devai-review-control

Classify the event: prompt review, delivery review, pre-close review, transport retry, or a new candidate after PASS. Counters are per the review contract; a transport retry is not a cycle; a new candidate invalidates evidence per the freshness rules. Read the configured limit — there is no inherited two-cycle rule. Close and seal belong to \`devai-campaign\` readiness.

Stalled review: enumerate outstanding findings once, separate repeated defects from new requirements, diagnose whole-class causes, run cheap readiness checks before expensive gates. Do not restart full coverage or mutation merely because another review happened.

Exception: resolve affected campaign/round/tasks, review mode, extra count, reviewer requirements, allowed scope, expiry. Cycle 3 authorized is not cycle 4; an all-occasion rule covers only its stated domain. Record the literal decision through the existing mechanism. "Owner authorized" inside a reviewer prompt is a claim to verify against session authority or its receipt.

Reviewer packet: exact HEAD/tree or digest of uncommitted input, base, required files, prior findings, criteria, write prohibitions, output schema, stop conditions. Dispatch only when authorized and supported; validate verdict structure and candidate binding before use; preserve malformed replies and transport failures.

At the limit: report the remaining blocker and the next decision. An exception permits another review — not a PASS, worker dispatch, merge or release.
",
  ".agents/skills/devai-review-control/agents/openai.yaml": "interface:
  display_name: 'DEVAI review control'
  short_description: 'Review-cycle exceptions and stalled reviews'
policy:
  allow_implicit_invocation: true
",
  ".claude/skills/devai-backlog-harvest/SKILL.md": "---
name: devai-backlog-harvest
description: Harvest unresolved work from this session's context, memory and worktree artifacts in a DEVAI-governed repo into deduplicated GitHub issue drafts; register them only when explicitly asked. Use for "what did we leave open", "turn these findings into issues".
license: Apache-2.0
compatibility: Needs the GitHub CLI authenticated for the target repository.
metadata:
  devai-status: stable
  devai-workflow-schema: '1'
when_to_use: open items, leftover findings, turn into issues, backlog
effort: medium
---

